  "vibe": "An oatmeal studio wall (#f1e9df) with terracotta (#b85c38) doing all the shouting, Gloock's high-contrast serif over Schibsted Grotesk captions. The backdrop is a wheel session in progress: a rust vessel that literally grows taller and wider across the beat while its shadow ellipse wobbles under it, a celadon zig-zag firing curve drawing itself in beneath the label \"cone 6 · 1222°C\", and three outlined pots standing on a drying shelf. Its signature beat is the drag — a chip pointer-dragged into a dashed slot that locks in with a tick — and its typing beat sets glaze notes word by word in tilted display serif. The camera drowses: slow 34px lifts, a half-degree roll, six unhurried moves. For ceramics studios, craft classes, makers' markets and any brand that wants patience to read as quality.",
